      "design": "r0B",
      "good": "Every date range, role, name and phone number stays intact. The week groups are particularly easy to identify.",
      "problems": "The notes become a narrow, tall strip of four- and five-line entries. The resulting row heights leave large areas of empty space under the contact details and make the schedule harder to scan as a whole.",
      "cause": "The 126px Week column accommodates the longest date range, but reduces Escalation notes to 157px."
    },
    {
      "design": "r0C",
      "good": "The wider notes column gives instructions a comfortable measure and makes the rows more even. Roles and phone numbers remain intact, and the compact table makes week-to-week comparison easier.",
      "problems": "All three date ranges split, and several engineer names wrap. The broken dates weaken the week labels, while wrapped names make the contact pair slightly slower to scan.",
      "cause": "The 85px Week column cannot hold the date ranges intact, and the 115px Engineer column cannot hold every full name."
    }
  ],
